# Build output. Both are fully generated — `lib/` by tsc, `build/` by the client
# compile — so nothing hand-written lives here and nothing here is worth a diff.
# `npm run prepare` regenerates them on install and before publish.
lib/
build/

# Dependencies. The DSH runtime packages are linked in from an existing DSH install
# by `scripts/link-runtime.mjs` (wired to `postinstall`), so this tree is machine
# state, not project state.
node_modules/

# Local-only documentation and logs. `.docs/` holds the design notes and the
# release-notes drafts; `.logs/` holds test, typecheck and web-run output. Neither
# is package content (`files` in package.json never includes them) and neither
# belongs in the repository.
.docs/
.logs/

# Local server logs from running the web profile against this checkout.
web-out.txt
web-err.txt
*.log

# Test fixtures. Most are named after the running process and removed when the suite
# exits, but a couple of suites build a fixed-name prefix that is meant to survive
# between runs. `test/` itself is tracked — it used to be ignored wholesale, which is
# how new test files were silently left out of the repository.
test/.fixtures/

# Pack artifacts.
*.tgz

# Scratch files. `commit-msg-tmp.txt` is written to pass a multi-paragraph commit
# message to `git commit -F` — PowerShell has no heredoc — and got itself committed
# twice because `git add -A` runs before `git commit -F` reads it. Ignoring the
# pattern is more reliable than remembering the ordering.
commit-msg-tmp.txt
.commit-msg.txt
.commit-msg.tmp
*.tmp
scratch-commit-msg.txt
scratch-msg.txt
tmp-commit-msg.txt
msg.txt
msg2.txt
msg3.txt
msg4.txt
msg5.txt
msg6.txt
msg7.txt

# Throwaway probe directories (`npm install` of a candidate library, one-off scripts).
# They are real files with a real node_modules, and while they were untracked the
# plugin's own delta engine reported them as "new files the index has not seen" —
# 19 of them at one point — which is exactly the noise the freshness signal cannot
# afford. The findings they produced live in `.docs/plan-0.1.10.md` §2.1.
.tmp-probe/
.tmp-npm-cache/

# A redirected `GITNEXUS_HOME` for sandboxed index runs (`analyze` writes its registry
# there). The registry is machine state, and while it was untracked the delta engine
# counted it as a file the index should have seen.
.tmp-gitnexus-home/
